# witness-only: EndpointProbeFailingBridge10m, EndpointProbeFailingMaxDirection, EndpointProbeFailingPre336
# EndpointProbeFailing — BOTH COPIES — lifted out of their manifests (comments and annotations
# stripped; the manifests are their one home) — the rules file that probes.promtool-test loads.
# Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules
# (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded
# directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY
# *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would fail it.
#
# ANNOTATIONS ARE STRIPPED deliberately, following gc-mirrors.promtool-rules and
# agents/scan-wedge-alert-test.sh: this pins FIRING BEHAVIOUR, not prose. The descriptions are
# runbooks and change on their own schedule; copying them here would give the runbook two homes.
#
# ⚠ NEITHER COPY IS DRIFT-PINNED — `devbox run exporter-self-test` pins only CiDispatchStalled. A
# stale copy tests the OLD expr and passes VACUOUSLY. Re-copy after editing either alert:
#
#   yq eval-all -o=json '[.] | map(select(.kind == "PrometheusRule")) | .[0] | {"groups": [{"name": "blackbox", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "EndpointProbeFailing") | del(.annotations)]}]}' \
#     argocd/resources/blackbox/blackbox.yaml | yq -P '.'
#   (one line on purpose — a wrapped yq program string is the #344 lexer bug; and eval-all +
#   kind-select because blackbox.yaml is MULTI-DOC — the old bare `.spec.groups[]` form silently
#   produced `rules: []` against it. Both verified by running the recipe and canonically diffing
#   against this file's blackbox group, 2026-08-12.)
#
# ⚠ THE `agentstack-slo-rendered` GROUP IS A HAND RENDER, and it is the one thing here a yq
# re-copy cannot produce. Its source is a Go template inside
# argocd/resources/agentstack/composition.yaml, which no tool in this repo can render offline
# (crossplane's function-go-templating runs in-cluster). It is transcribed with
# `$sloStack` = `oracle`, i.e. exactly what the live claim renders — `job="slo-oracle"`, verified
# against Prometheus 2026-08-12. The two copies are ONE alert in two files (#336) and the whole
# point of executing this group is that they cannot silently diverge; if you edit the template,
# edit this by hand in the same commit.
#
# THE TWO SHIPPED SELECTORS PARTITION THEIR TARGETS, which is why they can share this file and the
# alertname `EndpointProbeFailing` without colliding in exp_alerts: blackbox rule 1 takes
# `specs.oracle.*` only, rule 2 takes everything that is NOT `mcp|specs.oracle.*`, and the rendered
# composition rule takes `job="slo-oracle"` (the mcp endpoint). Every test below relies on that
# partition and asserts it — a series is expected to raise exactly one of the three.
groups:
  - name: blackbox
    rules:
      - alert: EndpointProbeFailing
        expr: min_over_time(probe_success{instance=~"https://specs\\.oracle\\..*"}[5m]) == 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          stack: oracle
      - alert: EndpointProbeFailing
        expr: min_over_time(probe_success{instance!~"https://(mcp|specs)\\.oracle\\..*"}[5m]) == 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning

  # ── The templated lane, hand-rendered at $sloStack = oracle (see the header) ──────────────────
  # ErrorBudgetBurnt and the stack:error_budget_burnt:bool recording rule that feeds it are NOT
  # here: #336 did not touch them (a 30d avg_over_time is already immune to the hole this class is
  # about, the same reason GithubStorageHeldHigh was left alone in #331). Named so the omission is
  # a known hole rather than an assumed pass.
  - name: agentstack-slo-rendered
    rules:
      - alert: EndpointProbeFailing
        expr: min_over_time(probe_success{job="slo-oracle"}[5m]) == 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          stack: oracle

  # ── REGRESSION WITNESS — NOT a deployed rule (the #310/#328/#335 device, homelab#336) ─────────
  # EndpointProbeFailing exactly as it shipped before #336: no hole half, no identity half (it
  # never needed one). It is the whole pre-fix alert, which is what keeps the contrast in
  # probes.promtool-test attributable to the bridge alone.
  # A FOSSIL, not a copy: if the shipped expr is revisited again, this stays as it is. It is also
  # what stops a stale hand copy of the groups above from passing vacuously — with the old expr in
  # both places the two agree and every hole assertion in the fixture fails.
  # One rule covers both shipped selectors: the tests drive it with one target at a time.
  - name: regression-witness-pre-336
    rules:
      - alert: EndpointProbeFailingPre336
        expr: probe_success == 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning

  # ── COUNTER-WITNESS — the mechanical [10m] port, the one #336 REFUSED ─────────────────────────
  # Not a fossil: this is the rule that would have shipped if the class block in
  # argocd/resources/github-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml had been applied to this alert by
  # substitution. It exists so #349's bound is EXECUTED rather than argued — on the 2026-08-07
  # 17:06Z flake replayed in probes.promtool-test it PAGES for an endpoint that missed two probes,
  # while the shipped [5m] expr stays silent through the same series. `for: 10m` is deliberately
  # identical: the range is the only variable.
  - name: counter-witness-bridge-10m
    rules:
      - alert: EndpointProbeFailingBridge10m
        expr: min_over_time(probe_success[10m]) == 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning

  # ── UnboundGithubServfail (homelab#1125) — DNS probe through Unbound for github names ────────
  # expr and for byte-identical to the CR in blackbox.yaml; annotations stripped per the
  # file convention (they are runbook prose, not firing behaviour).
  - name: unbound-github
    rules:
      - alert: UnboundGithubServfail
        expr: probe_success{instance="192.168.2.1:53",job="blackbox-unbound-github"} == 0
        for: 3m
        labels:
          severity: warning

  # ── DIRECTION WITNESS — `max_over_time`, the class's default and the wrong function here ──────
  # Class rule (ii) at GithubRateLimitLow: `max_over_time` is the alert-PRESERVING function only
  # where HIGH is the bad reading. `probe_success == 0` is the opposite, so max holds the
  # HEALTHIEST sample of the window and delays every page by the whole range. Executed in
  # probes.promtool-test rather than asserted in a comment.
  - name: direction-witness-max
    rules:
      - alert: EndpointProbeFailingMaxDirection
        expr: max_over_time(probe_success[5m]) == 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
